# The storage:link target, not content. On Windows it is a junction, so git walks
# it and commits a second copy of every upload. That copy checks out as a real
# directory on a Linux host, which makes storage:link a no-op and leaves fresh
# uploads 404ing. The files themselves are tracked under storage/app/public.
/public/storage
# Scratch uploads. Livewire parks every in-progress upload in livewire-tmp and
# sweeps it after a day; `imports` holds a copy of the sheet being imported for
# as long as the admin is on the page. Neither is content.
/storage/app/imports
/storage/app/public/livewire-tmp
/storage/*.key
/storage/pail
/vendor
_ide_helper.php
Homestead.json
Homestead.yaml
Thumbs.db

# bootstrap/cache/packages.php and services.php stay tracked, and nothing here
# may ever change them again. Laravel and composer rewrite both on every
# server, so the deployed copies are permanently modified against the repo — a
# commit that touches either path makes `git pull` abort with "your local
# changes would be overwritten", on a host where nobody can delete a file to
# clear it. Leaving them alone means git never has to touch them and the pull
# stays clean; `composer install` is what keeps the deployed copies correct.

# Catalogue PDF thumbnails, regenerated on demand.
/storage/app/catalogue-thumbs
